<?xml version='1.0' standalone='yes'?>
<!DOCTYPE PLUGIN>



<PLUGIN
  name="docktail-preview"
  author="vcolombo"
  version="2026.09.03.9.4"
  launch="Settings/DockTail"
  pluginURL="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/vcolombo/docktail-unraid/main/plugin/docktail-preview.plg"
  support="https://github.com/vcolombo/docktail-unraid/issues"
  min="7.0.0"
>

<CHANGES>
<![CDATA[

### 2026.09.03.9.4

Licensing compliance for the packaged binary.

The package shipped DockTail's compiled binary without the AGPL-3.0 licence text or any pointer to its source. It now installs `LICENSE` and `SOURCE` alongside the binary in `/usr/local/emhttp/plugins/docktail`, where `SOURCE` records the upstream repository, tag and exact commit the binary was built from.

No functional changes.

### 2026.09.03.9.3

Labels tab: enrolment view, name warnings, and un-enrolling.

- New **Enrolment** table lists every running container with its service name, funnel state and whether DockTail labels are present. The container picker marks enrolled containers too.
- Reusing a service name now warns, naming the container that already uses it. Two containers advertising one Service undo each other on every reconcile pass. It is advisory only, since reuse is legitimate when replacing a container.
- New **Remove DockTail labels** button produces the container's Extra Parameters with the DockTail labels stripped and everything else preserved - the supported way to un-enrol a container.

### 2026.09.03.9.2

Fixes a misleading message after a restart.

Restarting drains every Service, so for up to one reconcile interval afterwards nothing is advertised. The page reported that as "This Tailscale version does not report Services as JSON" - a wrong diagnosis of a normal, temporary state.

- An empty serve config is now recognised as nothing being advertised, not as a Tailscale limitation.
- When the service is running but Services have not returned yet, the page explains the reconcile delay.
- Start and Restart now say that Services re-advertise on the next reconcile pass.
- The raw-output fallback is reserved for output that genuinely cannot be parsed, and says only that.


For older releases, see https://github.com/vcolombo/docktail-unraid/releases
]]>
</CHANGES>

<FILE Name="/boot/config/plugins/docktail/docktail-unraid-2026.09.03.9.4-noarch-1.txz">
<URL>https://github.com/vcolombo/docktail-unraid/releases/download/2026.09.03.9.4/docktail-unraid-2026.09.03.9.4-noarch-1.txz</URL>
<SHA256>8076ef87196ae7549e4db87f6086033749e9a5bd7f043c564cc4ba563c519db9</SHA256>
</FILE>

<!--
The 'install' script. Unraid re-installs every /boot/config/plugins/*.plg on
boot, so this runs at boot too: it must be idempotent and must not fail when
Docker or Tailscale are still down.
-->
<FILE Run="/bin/bash">
<INLINE>
<![CDATA[
if [ -d "/usr/local/emhttp/plugins/docktail" ]; then
    rm -rf /usr/local/emhttp/plugins/docktail
fi

upgradepkg --install-new /boot/config/plugins/docktail/docktail-unraid-2026.09.03.9.4-noarch-1.txz

mkdir -p /boot/config/plugins/docktail

# Keep tailnet credentials out of Unraid Connect's flash backup, which is a git
# repo at /boot/.git.
echo "credentials.cfg" > /boot/config/plugins/docktail/.gitignore

if [ ! -f "/boot/config/plugins/docktail/credentials.cfg" ]; then
    install -m 0600 /dev/null /boot/config/plugins/docktail/credentials.cfg
fi
chmod 0600 /boot/config/plugins/docktail/credentials.cfg

# Drop the other release channel so both are never installed at once.
rm -f /boot/config/plugins/docktail.plg
rm -f /var/log/plugins/docktail.plg

# Start (or restart) the daemon. Deferred, so a blocking Unraid event returns
# immediately.
/usr/local/emhttp/plugins/docktail/restart.sh

# Clean up superseded packages.
rm -f $(ls /boot/config/plugins/docktail/docktail-unraid-*.txz 2>/dev/null | grep -v '2026.09.03.9.4')

echo ""
echo "----------------------------------------------------"
echo " docktail-preview has been installed."
echo " Plugin version:   2026.09.03.9.4"
echo " DockTail version: 1.7.9"
echo ""
echo " Configure it under Settings -> Network Services ->"
echo " DockTail. DockTail needs the Tailscale plugin and a"
echo " tagged Unraid node; the Status tab checks both."
echo "----------------------------------------------------"
echo ""
]]>
</INLINE>
</FILE>

<!--
The 'remove' script. Settings under /boot/config/plugins/docktail are left in place:
Unraid convention is that plugin settings survive removal.
-->
<FILE Run="/bin/bash" Method="remove">
<INLINE>
<![CDATA[
/usr/local/etc/rc.d/rc.docktail stop 2>/dev/null

removepkg docktail-unraid

rm -rf /usr/local/emhttp/plugins/docktail
rm -f /boot/config/plugins/docktail/*.txz
]]>
</INLINE>
</FILE>

</PLUGIN>
